---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { LINKS, href } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="What I build, how I work, and where else to find me."
>
	<header class="page-head">
		<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
		<h1>Short version: I build small tools.</h1>
	</header>

	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			I'm a full-stack developer working across Swift/macOS and TypeScript. Most of what I
			build sits close to the desktop — editors, utilities, and the plumbing that lets an
			agent do something useful inside them.
		</p>

		<p>
			I like small tools, clear interfaces, and systems that can explain themselves. That
			last part is most of the reason this site exists: writing things down is how I work
			out whether I actually understand them.
		</p>

		<h2>What I'm building</h2>

		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Meditor</strong> — a native macOS Markdown editor with a built-in AI agent.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>agentia</strong> — a declarative framework for agent services, with tracing
				and cost observability.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>How I work</h2>

		<p>
			Design sketch first, then a failing test, then the smallest change that makes it pass.
			Claims about behaviour get checked against the running thing rather than argued from
			the diff. When something breaks, the interesting question is usually why nothing
			caught it.
		</p>

		<blockquote>
			<p>If a system can't explain what it did, it isn't finished.</p>
		</blockquote>

		<h2>Elsewhere</h2>

		<ul>
			{
				LINKS.map((link) => (
					<li>
						<a href={link.href}>{link.label}</a>
					</li>
				))
			}
			<li>
				<a href={href('/rss.xml')}>RSS</a> — if you'd rather read this in a feed reader.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.page-head {
		margin-bottom: 2.4rem;
	}

	.page-head h1 {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
</style>
